  "review_lenses": {
    "architecture": "Runtime-ready handle loss observation and registry ownership stay in reusable JavaScript. Profile records transitions; no component, DOM protocol, or server authority added.",
    "implementation": "Latched loss before subscription rejects activation; active loss synchronously leaves ready; token-bound observers exclude obsolete handles, replacement loss rejects replay, and intentional stop clears observers.",
    "conformance": "Eight new real-startup/registry injected-frame tests plus five active scenarios per browser; repeated Phase 6 conformance and Phase 7 measurements passed. Controlled failure callbacks are not OS crashes.",
    "accessibility": "No semantic or focus contract change. Existing BH-02 evidence remains inherited; manual AT and native role gaps remain unclosed.",
    "security": "Existing acquisition, compatibility and correlated generation checks retained. Test-only browser instrumentation is route-injected, never shipped in profile assets. Production security/release review remains due.",
    "packaging": "No dependency or toolkit change. AtomVM-in-Wasm executes the pinned AVM bundle; all original artifact checks and pinned Mix/runtime tests repeated.",
    "provenance": "Each retained run names full Section 9.3 revision. Current runtime sources are checked against that git tree and SHA-256. Historical exception helper is restricted to exact authorized paths and a hash-bound authorization."
  },
